1
00:00:04,421 --> 00:00:07,382
You know how l feel about Halloween.

2
00:00:25,401 --> 00:00:26,609
-Who are you?
-Castiel.

3
00:00:26,777 --> 00:00:28,611
-What are you?
CASTlEL: An angel of the Lord.

4
00:00:28,779 --> 00:00:32,865
The Rising of the Witnesses
is one of the 66 seals.

5
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:36,369
Those seals are being broken by Lilith.

6
00:00:36,537 --> 00:00:39,080
-Last one opens and...?
-Lucifer walks free.

7
00:00:39,248 --> 00:00:41,416
DEAN: So you've been
using your freaky ESP stuff?

8
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:43,626
SAM: No.
-Well, let's keep it that way.

9
00:00:43,836 --> 00:00:45,294
SAM:
I'm just exorcising demons.

10
00:00:45,462 --> 00:00:47,797
DEAN: With your mind!
SAM: l can send them back to hell.

11
00:00:47,965 --> 00:00:50,049
-Try to see the other side.
-The other side?

12
00:00:50,217 --> 00:00:52,260
I'm pulling demons
out of innocent people.

13
00:00:52,428 --> 00:00:54,637
-Use the knife.
SAM: The knife kills the victim.

14
00:00:54,847 --> 00:00:56,431
What l do, most of them survive.

15
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:58,975
You should show me some respect.

16
00:00:59,143 --> 00:01:03,813
I dragged you out of hell.
I can throw you back in.

17
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:12,613
[PEOPLE CHATTERlNG]

18
00:01:16,869 --> 00:01:18,828
GIRL 1 : Throw them out?
GIRL 2: Yeah, pour it out.

19
00:01:18,996 --> 00:01:20,997
GIRL 1 :
Oh, yeah, put that on top. That's cool.

20
00:01:21,165 --> 00:01:22,749
GIRL 2:
Put it on the side.

21
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:29,672
-How was the store?
-Oh, madness.

22
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:30,840
Yeah.

23
00:01:31,008 --> 00:01:33,342
Everyone in town was stocking up.
Hi, sweet pea.

24
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:36,345
Did you get enough?

25
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:39,307
I had to arm-wrestle
Norma Bleeker for these.

26
00:01:39,475 --> 00:01:43,352
-Honey, she's 74.
-And a lot stronger than she looks.

27
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:44,645
Eh-eh-eh.

28
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:46,773
Remember last year? We ran out at 6:30.

29
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:49,192
-lt's just one piece.
-Eh-eh-eh. You can have...

30
00:01:49,401 --> 00:01:52,904
...as much as you want after Halloween.

31
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:54,697
-Come on.
-No.

32
00:01:54,907 --> 00:01:57,200
Who needs a bath?

33
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:59,869
Huh? Huh?

34
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:02,872
There we go. You coming?

35
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,540
Yeah. l'll be up in a minute.

36
00:02:04,708 --> 00:02:06,417
Okay.

37
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:07,835
Where's Mommy?

38
00:03:09,773 --> 00:03:12,900
Luke? What's taking you so long?

39
00:03:16,446 --> 00:03:18,781
[SCREAMS]

40
00:03:28,292 --> 00:03:30,960
Now, how many razor blades
did they find?

41
00:03:32,796 --> 00:03:35,965
Two on the floor, one in his stomach...

42
00:03:36,133 --> 00:03:38,968
...and one was stuck in his throat.

43
00:03:39,928 --> 00:03:43,431
He swallowed four of them.
How is that even possible?

44
00:03:47,895 --> 00:03:50,146
The candy was never in the oven.

45
00:03:52,649 --> 00:03:54,650
We just have to be thorough,
Mrs. Wallace.

46
00:03:54,818 --> 00:03:57,278
Did police find razors
in the rest of the candy?

47
00:03:57,446 --> 00:04:00,615
No. I mean, I don't know.
I don't think so.

48
00:04:02,075 --> 00:04:03,743
I just....

49
00:04:04,745 --> 00:04:07,163
I can't believe it.

50
00:04:07,456 --> 00:04:11,751
You hear urban legends about this stuff,
but it actually happens?

51
00:04:12,628 --> 00:04:15,129
SAM:
More than you might imagine.

52
00:04:20,594 --> 00:04:23,596
Mrs. Wallace, did Luke have any enemies?

53
00:04:23,764 --> 00:04:25,014
Enemies?

54
00:04:25,182 --> 00:04:27,183
Anyone who might've held a grudge?

55
00:04:27,351 --> 00:04:30,686
-What do you mean?
-Coworkers, neighbors.

56
00:04:33,857 --> 00:04:34,982
Maybe a woman.

57
00:04:36,610 --> 00:04:38,861
Are you suggesting an affair?

58
00:04:39,029 --> 00:04:41,197
-ls it possible?
-No.

59
00:04:41,365 --> 00:04:42,865
No, Luke would nev--

60
00:04:43,033 --> 00:04:46,702
I'm very sorry.
We just have to consider all possibilities.

61
00:04:47,454 --> 00:04:51,207
If someone wanted to kill my husband,
don't you think...

62
00:04:51,375 --> 00:04:55,336
...they'd find a better way than a razor
in a piece of candy he might eat?

63
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:11,560
Really?

64
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:14,146
After that guy choked
down all those razor blades?

65
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:15,731
It's Halloween, man.

66
00:05:15,899 --> 00:05:19,402
Yeah. For us, every day is Halloween.

67
00:05:19,569 --> 00:05:21,737
Don't be a downer. Anything interesting?

68
00:05:21,905 --> 00:05:24,573
Well, we're on a witch-hunt,
that's for sure, but this...

69
00:05:24,741 --> 00:05:26,742
...isn't your typical hex bag.

70
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:28,744
-No?
-Goldthread.

71
00:05:28,912 --> 00:05:31,080
An herb that's been extinct for 200 years.

72
00:05:31,248 --> 00:05:32,415
And this is Celtic.

73
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:34,667
And l don't mean
some New-Age knockoff.

74
00:05:34,835 --> 00:05:38,671
It looks like the real deal,
like 600-years-old real.

75
00:05:38,839 --> 00:05:43,759
And that is the charred
metacarpal bone of a newborn baby.

76
00:05:43,927 --> 00:05:46,095
-Oh. Gross.
-Relax, man.

77
00:05:46,263 --> 00:05:47,930
It's at least a hundred years old.

78
00:05:48,098 --> 00:05:51,851
Oh, right, like that makes it better.
Witches, man, so frigging skeevy.

79
00:05:52,019 --> 00:05:55,438
Yeah. Well, takes a pretty powerful one
to put a bag like this together.

80
00:05:55,647 --> 00:05:57,440
More juice than we've ever dealt with.

81
00:05:57,649 --> 00:05:59,275
Find anything on the victim?

82
00:05:59,443 --> 00:06:03,279
This Luke Wallace, he was so vanilla,
that he made vanilla seem spicy.

83
00:06:05,032 --> 00:06:08,409
I can't find any reason why somebody
would want this guy dead.

84
00:06:09,286 --> 00:06:11,454
[MUSlC PLAYS OVER SPEAKERS]

85
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:13,706
[CHATTERlNG]

86
00:06:14,124 --> 00:06:15,750
Hey.

87
00:06:16,668 --> 00:06:19,754
This party blows.

88
00:06:19,963 --> 00:06:21,422
We should just go tp somebody.

89
00:06:24,259 --> 00:06:25,760
-Hey, Justin.
-Yo.

90
00:06:25,927 --> 00:06:27,428
TRACY:
You break into the booze yet?

91
00:06:28,472 --> 00:06:30,556
It's triple-locked.

92
00:06:30,891 --> 00:06:33,726
So you guys going to the
mausoleum party tomorrow night?

93
00:06:33,894 --> 00:06:35,227
Are you gonna be there?

94
00:06:35,896 --> 00:06:39,065
It's gonna be rad.
I'm gonna get so baked.

95
00:06:39,274 --> 00:06:42,318
Well, it's gotta be better
than this G-rated ass-fest.

96
00:06:42,486 --> 00:06:44,070
Oh, come on, it's not that bad.

97
00:06:45,781 --> 00:06:47,323
Oh, check it out.

98
00:06:48,408 --> 00:06:49,825
Okay, bobbing for apples is lame.

99
00:06:50,494 --> 00:06:53,454
-Oh, come on. It's Halloween.
-Eh.... Lame.

100
00:07:06,009 --> 00:07:07,093
I stand corrected.

101
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:10,679
Well, l wanna try.

102
00:07:32,744 --> 00:07:35,287
Wow. She can really hold her breath.

103
00:07:42,629 --> 00:07:44,046
Jenny?

104
00:07:46,216 --> 00:07:48,050
Help me.

105
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:50,636
Jenny, what's wrong? Help!

106
00:07:51,847 --> 00:07:53,389
Come on, let's go.

107
00:07:59,563 --> 00:08:02,356
-What is happening?
-Jenny, come on!

108
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:06,402
[SCREAMlNG]

109
00:08:10,407 --> 00:08:12,408
Help. Jenny!

110
00:08:13,243 --> 00:08:16,287
Jenny. Jenny.

111
00:08:21,877 --> 00:08:24,044
JUSTlN:
Oh, my God.

112
00:08:35,432 --> 00:08:37,516
-Have you been drinking tonight?
-Yes.

113
00:08:38,185 --> 00:08:40,269
-l got this one.
TRACY: The water started boiling.

114
00:08:40,437 --> 00:08:42,688
Two words: Jail, bait.

115
00:08:42,856 --> 00:08:44,773
I would never.

116
00:08:47,611 --> 00:08:49,111
TRACY:
You know, it's just so weird.

117
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:52,239
The water in the tub, it wasn't hot.

118
00:08:52,407 --> 00:08:53,949
I had just been in there myself.

119
00:08:54,117 --> 00:08:57,119
Your friend didn't happen to know
a man named Luke Wallace.

120
00:08:57,621 --> 00:09:00,247
Agent Seger, FBI.

121
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:02,541
Um, who's Luke Wallace?

122
00:09:04,211 --> 00:09:05,544
He died yesterday.

123
00:09:06,463 --> 00:09:07,630
I don't know who that is.

124
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:25,439
I'm telling you,
both of these vics are clean.

125
00:09:25,607 --> 00:09:27,816
There is no reason
for wicked-bitch payback.

126
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:30,152
Maybe because it's not about that.

127
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:31,403
Wow, insightful.

128
00:09:31,571 --> 00:09:33,781
Maybe this witch isn't working a grudge.

129
00:09:33,949 --> 00:09:36,116
Maybe they're working a spell.
Check this out:

130
00:09:36,284 --> 00:09:38,327
"Three blood sacrifices over three days.

131
00:09:38,495 --> 00:09:43,415
The last before midnight
on the final day of the final harvest."

132
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:47,795
Celtic calendar, the final day
of the final harvest is October 31 st.

133
00:09:47,963 --> 00:09:49,296
-Halloween.
-Exactly.

134
00:09:50,674 --> 00:09:52,800
What exactly are the blood sacrifices for?

135
00:09:52,968 --> 00:09:55,469
SAM: Well, if I'm right,
this witch is summoning a demon.

136
00:09:55,637 --> 00:09:57,513
And not just any demon.

137
00:09:57,681 --> 00:09:59,014
Samhain.

138
00:09:59,182 --> 00:10:03,519
-Am I supposed to be impressed?
-Samhain is the origin of Halloween.

139
00:10:03,687 --> 00:10:05,771
The Celts believed
that October 31st was...

140
00:10:05,939 --> 00:10:09,024
...when the veil was
thinnest between the living and dead.

141
00:10:09,192 --> 00:10:12,027
It was Samhain's night.
Masks were put on to hide from him.

142
00:10:12,195 --> 00:10:14,154
Sweets left on doorsteps to appease him.

143
00:10:14,322 --> 00:10:16,365
Faces carved
into pumpkins to worship him.

144
00:10:16,533 --> 00:10:18,367
He was exorcised centuries ago.

145
00:10:18,535 --> 00:10:21,203
Samhain took a trip downstairs,
the traditions stuck.

146
00:10:21,413 --> 00:10:24,456
Exactly. Only now,
instead of demons and blood orgies...

147
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:27,209
...Halloween is all
about kids, candy and costumes.

148
00:10:27,544 --> 00:10:30,796
Okay, so some witch wants to raise
Samhain and take back the night?

149
00:10:30,964 --> 00:10:32,715
-Dean, this is serious.
-l am serious.

150
00:10:32,924 --> 00:10:34,717
We're talking heavyweight witchcraft.

151
00:10:34,884 --> 00:10:37,219
This can only be performed
every 600 years.

152
00:10:37,387 --> 00:10:39,221
And the 600-year marker rolls around--

153
00:10:39,431 --> 00:10:41,140
-Tomorrow night.
-Naturally.

154
00:10:41,308 --> 00:10:43,183
Sure is a lot of of death for one demon.

155
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:44,727
Because he likes company.

156
00:10:44,936 --> 00:10:47,646
Once he's raised,
Samhain can do some raising of his own.

157
00:10:47,814 --> 00:10:50,816
-Raising what, exactly?
-Dark, evil crap, and lots of it.

158
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:53,068
They follow him around
like the pied piper.

159
00:10:53,236 --> 00:10:54,737
DEAN: We're talking ghosts?
-Yeah.

160
00:10:54,904 --> 00:10:55,904
-Zombies?
-Mm-hm.

161
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:57,197
-Leprechauns?
-Dean.

162
00:10:57,365 --> 00:10:59,366
Those little dudes are scary. Small hands.

163
00:10:59,534 --> 00:11:03,912
Look, it just starts with ghosts
and ghouls. This sucker keeps on going.

164
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:07,416
By night's end, we are talking
every awful thing we've ever seen.

165
00:11:07,584 --> 00:11:10,502
Everything we fight. All in one place.

166
00:11:12,714 --> 00:11:14,590
It's gonna be a slaughterhouse.

167
00:11:32,442 --> 00:11:35,402
[PHONE PLAYlNG ROCK MUSlC]

168
00:11:39,407 --> 00:11:41,408
-Hey.
-How's it going?

169
00:11:41,576 --> 00:11:44,286
Awesome. Yeah, I talked
to Mrs. Razor Blade again.

170
00:11:44,454 --> 00:11:48,457
I've been in front of her house for hours
and l've got a big steamy pile of nothing.

171
00:11:48,625 --> 00:11:51,960
Someone planted those hex bags,
someone with access to both houses.

172
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:54,505
-Gotta be some connection.
-l hope we find it...

173
00:11:54,672 --> 00:11:58,050
...because I'm starting to cramp like a--
Son of a bitch.

174
00:11:59,135 --> 00:12:00,177
Quit whining.

175
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:03,639
No, Sam, l mean, son of a bitch.

176
00:12:05,475 --> 00:12:07,810
-Hey.
-Hi.

177
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:14,024
So? Our apple-bobbing cheerleader?

178
00:12:14,192 --> 00:12:16,693
Tracy, the Wallace's babysitter.

179
00:12:16,861 --> 00:12:19,696
She told me she'd
never even heard of Luke Wallace.

180
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:23,158
Interesting look for a centuries-old witch.

181
00:12:23,326 --> 00:12:26,370
If you were a 600-year-old hag
and you could pick any costume...

182
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:29,373
...to come back in,
wouldn't you go for a hot cheerleader?

183
00:12:30,667 --> 00:12:31,834
I would.

184
00:12:33,711 --> 00:12:35,504
Mm.

185
00:12:41,136 --> 00:12:43,637
Well, Tracy's not as wholesome
as she looks.

186
00:12:43,805 --> 00:12:45,180
Did some digging.

187
00:12:45,348 --> 00:12:48,851
Apparently, she got into a violent
altercation with one of her teachers.

188
00:12:49,018 --> 00:12:50,227
Got suspended from school.

189
00:13:03,199 --> 00:13:08,036
[PEOPLE SCREAMING
IN VOlCE-OVER]

190
00:13:09,539 --> 00:13:10,831
SAM:
Bring back memories?

191
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:13,542
What do you mean?

192
00:13:13,710 --> 00:13:17,588
-Being a teenager, all that angst.
-Oh.

193
00:13:17,755 --> 00:13:21,175
-What'd you think l meant?
-Nothing.

194
00:13:21,885 --> 00:13:24,553
MAN: Fifteen minutes.
WOMAN: That's all?

195
00:13:24,721 --> 00:13:26,930
Now, that brings back memories.

196
00:13:27,432 --> 00:13:30,058
Dude, I need a bigger kiln.

197
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:32,769
HARDlNG:
You gentlemen wanna talk to me?

198
00:13:32,937 --> 00:13:35,689
SAM: Mr. Harding.
-Oh, please, Don.

199
00:13:35,857 --> 00:13:38,275
SAM: Okay. Don.
-Even my students call me Don.

200
00:13:38,443 --> 00:13:40,152
DEAN:
Yeah, we get it, Don.

201
00:13:40,778 --> 00:13:42,571
I'm Agent Geddy. This is Agent Lee.

202
00:13:42,739 --> 00:13:45,407
We just had
a few questions about Tracy Davis.

203
00:13:45,575 --> 00:13:49,912
Yeah, Tracy. Bright kid, loads of talent.
It's a shame she got suspended.

204
00:13:50,079 --> 00:13:53,081
You two had a violent altercation?

205
00:13:53,249 --> 00:13:56,793
Yeah, she exploded. lf Principal Morrow
hadn't walked by when he did...

206
00:13:56,961 --> 00:13:58,462
...Tracy would've clawed my eyes out.

207
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:00,756
-Why?
-l was only trying...

208
00:14:00,924 --> 00:14:02,591
...to rap with her about her work.

209
00:14:02,759 --> 00:14:05,093
It had gotten inappropriate
and disturbing.

210
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:09,681
More disturbing than those guys?

211
00:14:11,309 --> 00:14:15,437
She would cover page after page
with these bizarre, cryptic symbols.

212
00:14:15,605 --> 00:14:17,814
And then there were the drawings.

213
00:14:17,982 --> 00:14:23,070
Detailed images of killings.
Gory, primitive.

214
00:14:23,238 --> 00:14:27,491
She would depict herself
in the middle of them, participating.

215
00:14:28,701 --> 00:14:32,621
Symbols? What kind of symbols?
Anything like this?

216
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:36,750
Yeah. l think that might've been
one of them.

217
00:14:37,210 --> 00:14:39,795
-Know where Tracy is now?
-l imagine at her apartment.

218
00:14:39,963 --> 00:14:40,963
Her apartment?

219
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:43,674
Yeah. She got here
about a year ago, alone.

220
00:14:43,841 --> 00:14:46,260
As l understood it,
as an emancipated teen.

221
00:14:46,928 --> 00:14:49,471
God only knows
what her parents were like.

222
00:14:58,147 --> 00:15:00,774
DEAN: So?
SAM: Tracy was nowhere l could find.

223
00:15:00,942 --> 00:15:03,360
-Any luck with her friends?
-Luck is not our style.

224
00:15:03,528 --> 00:15:05,696
Friends don't know where she is.

225
00:15:05,863 --> 00:15:07,823
She could be making the third sacrifice.

226
00:15:07,991 --> 00:15:10,033
Yes, thank you, Sam.

227
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:12,494
Trick or treat?

228
00:15:12,662 --> 00:15:14,955
-This is a motel.
-So?

229
00:15:15,665 --> 00:15:17,040
So we don't have any candy.

230
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:20,168
-No, we have a ton in the--
-We did, but it's gone.

231
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:25,340
-Sorry, kid, we can't help you.
-l want candy.

232
00:15:25,508 --> 00:15:28,176
Well, l think you've had enough.

233
00:15:38,688 --> 00:15:40,230
Who are you?

234
00:15:40,398 --> 00:15:42,316
DEAN:
Sam. Sam, wait!

235
00:15:42,775 --> 00:15:46,320
That's Castiel. The angel.

236
00:15:47,405 --> 00:15:49,489
Him, I don't know.

237
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:52,868
Hello, Sam.

238
00:15:53,036 --> 00:15:58,040
Oh, my God. Or, uh.... I didn't mean to--
Sorry. lt's an honor.

239
00:15:58,583 --> 00:16:01,209
Really. l've heard a lot about you.

240
00:16:07,175 --> 00:16:08,717
And l you.

241
00:16:10,094 --> 00:16:14,306
Sam Winchester,
the boy with the demon blood.

242
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:19,686
Glad to hear you've ceased
your extracurricular activities.

243
00:16:19,854 --> 00:16:21,188
URIEL:
Let's keep it that way.

244
